# Firmware

- ESP-IDF C in `firmware/node/` (`aeios_bsp` / `hal` / `drivers` / `amp` / `services` / `app`). ADR-002 stands. No parallel PlatformIO/C++ tree.
- Explicit drivers: PMS5003, SCD41, BME688, MQ135, SX1278. No GPS driver.
- Layers: driver → normalized observation → intelligence. Packet codec ≠ radio driver. Policy ≠ driver.
- MQ135 heater FSM; raw ADC is not ppm. BME688 gas is a feature, not ppm.
- Quality flags survive into packets. AMP ACK/NACK/retry retained (C-08).
- Bring-up: ADR-013 (power → BSP → I²C → SCD41/BME688 → PMS → MQ135 → LoRa → intelligence). No GPS. No indefinite blocking.
- Deterministic adaptive policy on node; no TFLite (ADR-017).
- Host-testable mocks; production-disabled fault injection.

This rule does not override FAS; pin/driver names follow ADR-013 until FAS is revised.
